## Why This Is Asked
Tests building a low-latency, privacy-preserving NLP service with in-VPC explainability and PrivateLink access to a private data lake. It also probes rollout strategy and cost awareness.

## Key Concepts
- Low-latency NLP inference on a small multilingual LM
- In-container explainability (Integrated Gradients) within a VPC
- PrivateLink access to data lake and Redis cache in VPC
- Canary rollouts with rollback on latency drift or metric drop
- Cost controls and autoscaling policies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-invocation of inference+explanation
async function inferWithExplain(input) {
  const pred = await callEndpoint(input);
  const expl = await callExplainService(input, pred);
  return { pred, expl };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test latency and explainability under burst load?
- What rollback criteria would you codify in the deployment pipeline?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-tenant orchestration, real-time streaming inference, private isolation via PrivateLink, and drift-aware canaries across tenants.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Model Registry and Pipelines for per-tenant versioning
- PrivateLink and VPC isolation
- Per-tenant feature gating and rate limiting
- Drift detection using per-tenant feature distributions (Feature Store) and latency metrics
- Canary rollout governance with automatic rollback
- Cost modeling per tenant and region

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo routing and canary logic per tenant
function chooseModelForTenant(tenantId, payload) {
  const meta = loadTenantMeta(tenantId);
  const useCandidate = meta.canaryActive && Math.random() < meta.canaryTraffic;
  const model = useCandidate ? meta.candidateModel : meta.currentModel;
  return model.predict(payload);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant isolation in a shared endpoint?
- How would you monitor drift with streaming data?
- How do you escalate or rollback a tenant canary automatically when SLA is breached?

## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates expertise in deploying real-time ML systems within AWS for privacy-sensitive, multi-tenant environments requiring comprehensive monitoring, explainability, and rapid recovery capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- AWS PrivateLink and SageMaker endpoint architecture
- Private data lake integration with strict multi-tenant isolation
- Real-time drift detection and SHAP/IG explainability frameworks
- Provisioned concurrency and autoscaling for performance targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Explainer integration for inference transparency
function explainInference(model, input, featureNames) {
  const shapValues = model.predictSHAP(input);
  const igValues = model.predictIntegratedGradients(input);
  return {
    prediction: model.predict(input),
    explanations: {
      shap: shapValues,
      integratedGradients: igValues,
      featureNames: featureNames
    },
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    tenantId: extractTenantId(input)
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of explainability and governance as essential components of production ML workflows, not just model performance.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Clarify for feature attributions and bias detection
- Model Registry and Pipelines for full traceability and lineage
- Lightweight dashboards (QuickSight) for non-technical stakeholders
- Drift detection and automated rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Call SageMaker Clarify for per-inference feature attributions
const explanation = await clarify.explain({
  model: 'sentiment-classifier-v1',
  data: { text: 'This product is amazing!' }
});

// Retrieve bias score
const biasReport = await clarify.getBiasScore({
  model: 'sentiment-classifier-v1',
  dataset: 'production-reviews'
});

// Register model with explanations
await modelRegistry.register({
  modelName: 'sentiment-classifier-v1',
  explanations: explanation,
  biasScore: biasReport
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical use of SageMaker multi-model endpoints, per-tenant routing, and controlled releases under data privacy constraints (PrivateLink). It blends model choice, infrastructure sizing, and a measurable validation plan suitable for entry-level engineers.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker multi-model endpoints and Model Registry
- Tenant-aware routing with API Gateway + Lambda
- PrivateLink data isolation and VPC considerations
- Canary rollouts and rollback criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for tenant routing to a variant
function routeTenant(req){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  const variant = registry.getVariant(tenant);
  return endpoint.invoke({Body: req.body, Variant: variant});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test tenant isolation in practice?
- How would you monitor per-tenant drift and trigger rollbacks?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect per-tenant, private data path while supporting burst workloads, with per-tenant model versions, canary rollouts, and drift monitoring in AWS ML services.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Multi-Model Endpoint
- PrivateLink data residency
- Per-tenant Model Registry tags
- Canary rollouts and tenant routing
- Drift detection with SageMaker Clarify

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo AWS SDK calls to register and route per-tenant models
const sm = new SageMaker({region: 'us-east-1'});
sm.registerModel({ModelName:'tenantA-v2', ...});
sm.createEndpoint({EndpointName:'multi-tenant-endpoint', ...});

// Lambda routing logic
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const tenant = event.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const modelName = `${tenant}-latest`;
  return await sm.invokeEndpoint({
    EndpointName: 'multi-tenant-endpoint',
    TargetModel: modelName,
    Body: JSON.stringify(event.body)
  });
};
```
